      correct: 2,
      explanation: 'In the SHORT RUN, a perfectly competitive firm cannot change its fixed costs — they are sunk. If the market price is above the shutdown point (P > AVC) but below average total cost (P < ATC), the firm cannot earn a profit but can minimise its losses. It does so by producing the output level where MR = MC (marginal revenue equals marginal cost), which is the loss-minimising quantity. Fixed costs cannot be reduced in the short run (option B is wrong); in the long run, the firm would exit (option D) rather than "eliminate fixed costs."'
