      correct: 0,
      explanation: 'In the SHORT RUN, a firm facing losses has two choices: reduce production to the loss-minimising quantity (where MR = MC, if P > AVC) or shut down entirely (if P < AVC, meaning it cannot even cover variable costs). In the long run, the response to persistent losses is EXIT from the industry — not just "reducing production or shutting down." Short run: shutdown decision. Long run: exit decision.'
